FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/speech-to-text.1
    speech-to-text: writes what the microphone hears as text, in English:
    transcribe.cpp with NVIDIA's Parakeet model and Silero's voice detector.
    
      speech-to-text [MODEL.gguf [DETECTOR.gguf]]
    
    Words appear while they are spoken: the line is shown dim and revised until
    1.5 s without speech end it; after 15 s a breath ends it, at 30 s it ends
    anyway. Ctrl+C leaves. It needs microphone@0, and the browser asks for the
    microphone, which is open only while it listens. Nothing that is said leaves
    the page: the model runs in the session.
